WEBVTT

00:02:00.310 --> 00:02:04.210
We're all going home to the colony together

00:02:26.320 --> 00:02:28.460
It doesn't seem like there's any water anywhere.

00:02:29.210 --> 00:02:34.270
Luna!

00:02:39.150 --> 00:02:41.250
They said we should be ready to leave soon.

00:02:41.660 --> 00:02:42.370
Really?

00:02:54.450 --> 00:02:55.350
Shall we go back?

00:02:59.360 --> 00:03:00.410
Hey, Luna...

00:03:01.380 --> 00:03:06.150
My mom and dad were trying to bring this planet back to life, right?

00:03:06.630 --> 00:03:07.420
That's right.

00:03:07.760 --> 00:03:12.860
They wanted to make this a world where me and my kind could live, right?

00:03:13.500 --> 00:03:17.620
Yes. They seem like very kind people, so I'm sure that's true.

00:03:37.650 --> 00:03:39.410
I should show this to everyone!

00:03:46.570 --> 00:03:48.220
That sand is terrible!

00:03:49.080 --> 00:03:50.770
So, how was it?

00:03:51.560 --> 00:03:54.770
Well, the engine room's full'a sand too.

00:03:55.200 --> 00:03:56.360
Is it okay?

00:03:56.770 --> 00:04:00.120
By taking the sand out, we've made it so it'll run again.

00:04:00.860 --> 00:04:02.580
I hope it doesn't hinder the ship's operation.

00:04:03.070 --> 00:04:06.330
It shouldn't, but I don't feel great about it.

00:04:06.970 --> 00:04:08.400
It's so tedious.

00:04:08.960 --> 00:04:10.530
You keep working and working...

00:04:11.850 --> 00:04:13.080
...and there's no end to it.

00:04:13.530 --> 00:04:18.260
That's right. So long as we're in a desert, sand'll keep gettin' in.

00:04:18.930 --> 00:04:22.010
I hope the engine lasts until we get out of the desert.

00:04:27.110 --> 00:04:29.270
Hey, what do you mean by that?

00:04:30.330 --> 00:04:31.230
I just...

00:04:32.210 --> 00:04:35.960
What are we supposed to do if we break down in the middle of the desert?

00:04:36.110 --> 00:04:37.120
Well...

00:04:37.530 --> 00:04:39.480
Are we supposed to walk the rest of the way?

00:04:39.480 --> 00:04:40.990
Howard, stop it!

00:04:41.250 --> 00:04:42.970
It'll be okay, right?

00:04:42.970 --> 00:04:43.800
Stop that!

00:04:44.130 --> 00:04:45.110
Howard!

00:04:45.450 --> 00:04:46.080
Stop it.

00:04:46.080 --> 00:04:47.100
I said stop!

00:04:47.320 --> 00:04:49.120
Howard, stop it!

00:04:49.680 --> 00:04:51.970
If it breaks, me 'n Shingo'll fix it!

00:04:52.310 --> 00:04:53.750
You don't hafta worry 'bout it!

00:05:06.000 --> 00:05:07.760
Gravity control unit active.

00:05:08.280 --> 00:05:09.020
Lifting off!

00:05:35.730 --> 00:05:38.130
Is this all there is left?

00:05:42.480 --> 00:05:45.110
Our current location's around here.

00:05:45.820 --> 00:05:47.720
Our destination, the main computer...

00:05:50.100 --> 00:05:50.720
...is here.

00:05:51.330 --> 00:05:53.350
How long do you think before we can be there?

00:05:53.730 --> 00:05:54.900
If I had'ta say...

00:05:55.530 --> 00:05:58.530
...because'a the sand gettin' in, we're makin' slow progress...

00:05:58.870 --> 00:06:00.940
...so it might take two or three days.

00:06:01.460 --> 00:06:02.770
Two or three days...

00:06:03.520 --> 00:06:04.310
I see...

00:06:07.460 --> 00:06:08.580
Let's have lunch.

00:06:09.480 --> 00:06:10.530
I've been waitin'!

00:06:16.200 --> 00:06:17.170
Just this?

00:06:22.460 --> 00:06:24.110
Well, let's eat!

00:06:28.380 --> 00:06:29.550
I'll leave it here.

00:06:30.710 --> 00:06:31.500
Thanks.

00:06:33.750 --> 00:06:34.270
Huh?

00:06:36.300 --> 00:06:37.010
Sharla...

00:06:37.980 --> 00:06:39.440
We're one cup short.

00:06:40.270 --> 00:06:43.570
It's okay. I finished mine off while getting it ready.

00:06:44.700 --> 00:06:46.120
That's your share, Luna.

00:06:55.530 --> 00:06:57.410
Then I'll take it.

00:07:10.570 --> 00:07:12.260
Adam, what's wrong?

00:07:16.010 --> 00:07:18.820
Adam, make sure you eat it all up!

00:07:19.350 --> 00:07:22.650
You've only just gotten better, so you have to build up your strength.

00:07:23.100 --> 00:07:25.150
'at's right! Get eatin'!

00:07:37.980 --> 00:07:39.670
Hey, look at this!

00:07:51.630 --> 00:07:52.500
It's beautiful!

00:07:52.650 --> 00:07:54.220
Where'd that come from?

00:07:54.600 --> 00:07:56.620
I found it earlier in the desert.

00:07:56.880 --> 00:07:58.120
It looks like a flower, doesn't it?

00:07:58.870 --> 00:08:02.470
Minerals in the sand musta clumped together to form it.

00:08:04.310 --> 00:08:05.280
Really.

00:08:05.960 --> 00:08:07.120
Howard, look!

00:08:07.500 --> 00:08:08.320
Isn't it pretty?

00:08:10.830 --> 00:08:12.630
It really does look like a flower.

00:08:12.860 --> 00:08:14.280
Quite a lucky find.

00:08:15.450 --> 00:08:18.210
Don't you think it's wonderful to find a flower in the desert?

00:08:18.600 --> 00:08:20.100
A desert flower, huh?

00:08:21.220 --> 00:08:25.980
Maybe there's a flower patch somewhere in the desert, too!

00:08:26.730 --> 00:08:30.840
Sharla the fairy-tale girl, startin' up again!

00:08:31.200 --> 00:08:32.060
Chako!

00:08:32.880 --> 00:08:37.680
It's cool. A flower patch in the desert is mighty romantic.

00:08:38.210 --> 00:08:39.350
I'd like to go there.

00:08:40.720 --> 00:08:41.510
Me too.

00:08:42.000 --> 00:08:43.650
I'm sure it would be wonderful!

00:08:43.650 --> 00:08:44.700
Give me a break.

00:08:45.630 --> 00:08:48.320
This is no time to be having that kind of worthless conversation.

00:08:51.970 --> 00:08:55.530
If the Orion breaks down, what will happen to us?

00:08:55.800 --> 00:08:56.770
Howard!

00:08:56.810 --> 00:08:59.470
Can we make it through this desert by walking?

00:09:00.260 --> 00:09:03.450
There's no food or water -- it's obviously impossible!

00:09:03.820 --> 00:09:05.170
We'd die!

00:09:05.580 --> 00:09:06.920
Howard, stop it!

00:09:07.160 --> 00:09:11.280
When that happens, you can ramble on pointlessly about your desert flower patch!

00:09:11.730 --> 00:09:14.510
Who cares about a flower patch? Who cares about a desert flower?

00:09:16.830 --> 00:09:17.930
Take this!

00:09:25.570 --> 00:09:27.520
Howard, don't you get it?

00:09:28.500 --> 00:09:29.530
Get what?

00:09:30.260 --> 00:09:33.860
You're not to only anxious one, Howard. We're all afraid!

00:09:45.180 --> 00:09:50.810
That's why Sharla showed us this flower to cheer us up!

00:09:51.410 --> 00:09:54.550
She tried to start a fun conversation for once!

00:09:56.020 --> 00:09:56.960
Luna...

00:09:57.330 --> 00:10:00.560
No matter how worried we are, right now there's nothing we can do.

00:10:01.120 --> 00:10:04.560
All there is to do is go forward believing we'll ride it out!

00:10:05.280 --> 00:10:07.800
A real coward, ain't'cha?

00:10:10.230 --> 00:10:11.070
Howard!

00:10:12.220 --> 00:10:13.030
Wait!

00:10:16.350 --> 00:10:17.100
Here.

00:10:18.450 --> 00:10:19.230
Thanks.

00:10:20.920 --> 00:10:21.710
You see...

00:10:22.680 --> 00:10:23.880
What is it, Adam?

00:10:26.210 --> 00:10:28.610
Sharla... really...

00:10:30.150 --> 00:10:31.590
What about Sharla?

00:10:44.170 --> 00:10:45.030
Adam...?

00:11:00.330 --> 00:11:01.500
Howard...

00:11:06.030 --> 00:11:08.170
I'm always like this.

00:11:09.670 --> 00:11:11.700
I'm sorry for annoying you.

00:11:16.230 --> 00:11:20.970
I hope we can cross the desert and make it to the main computer.

00:11:24.480 --> 00:11:27.300
Let's go home to the colony together, Howard.

00:11:33.520 --> 00:11:35.700
Sharla, come here.

00:11:39.710 --> 00:11:40.950
Here, take it.

00:11:41.660 --> 00:11:43.200
Adam told me.

00:11:44.470 --> 00:11:46.680
Sharla, you haven't drank any water, have you?

00:11:47.880 --> 00:11:49.000
I'm fine.

00:11:49.570 --> 00:11:50.700
No, drink it.

00:11:51.370 --> 00:11:52.080
It's okay.

00:11:52.200 --> 00:11:58.200
It's not okay. Dividing your share among everyone else isn't fair to you, Sharla.

00:11:59.170 --> 00:12:01.720
It's not that I'm suffering through it.

00:12:02.100 --> 00:12:05.020
Even if I don't eat or drink for now, I'll be fine.

00:12:05.620 --> 00:12:08.690
And there's not much food or water left.

00:12:09.330 --> 00:12:11.610
But your strength will...

00:12:11.880 --> 00:12:15.450
Luna, I <i>am</i> thinking about my strength.

00:12:15.930 --> 00:12:18.610
When the time comes, I'll definitely drink. I promise.

00:12:19.610 --> 00:12:20.810
Sharla...

00:12:35.360 --> 00:12:36.300
This is bad.

00:12:37.010 --> 00:12:38.580
The wind's gotten more violent.

00:13:23.660 --> 00:13:25.220
I can hardly see straight ahead!

00:13:26.660 --> 00:13:29.170
The wind's getting stronger and stronger.

00:13:45.260 --> 00:13:48.150
The gravity control unit's output's unstable.

00:13:48.820 --> 00:13:50.730
It's probably the effect of the sand.

00:14:10.650 --> 00:14:11.730
What happened?

00:14:16.050 --> 00:14:18.230
Kaoru, the Gravity Control Unit...

00:14:19.720 --> 00:14:20.730
Is it done for?

00:14:21.480 --> 00:14:22.380
Hurry!

00:14:37.310 --> 00:14:38.770
It's the edge of the sandstorm!

00:15:26.770 --> 00:15:28.460
Adam, are you okay?

00:15:31.720 --> 00:15:32.390
Everyone?

00:15:32.850 --> 00:15:34.200
Yes, I'm fine.

00:15:35.660 --> 00:15:36.350
I'm okay.

00:15:36.820 --> 00:15:38.880
I'm alright, somehow.

00:15:40.310 --> 00:15:41.730
Everyone, you okay?

00:15:42.370 --> 00:15:44.280
Chako! How's Shingo?

00:15:45.220 --> 00:15:46.230
I'm fine!

00:15:46.870 --> 00:15:48.030
How are things down below?

00:15:49.760 --> 00:15:51.450
The gravity control unit...

00:15:51.450 --> 00:15:52.760
Will it run?

00:15:53.400 --> 00:15:54.630
We'll do somethin' 'bout it!

00:15:55.200 --> 00:15:56.170
Just wait!

00:16:01.120 --> 00:16:01.910
What's that?

00:16:09.000 --> 00:16:10.460
We definitely lurched just now.

00:16:14.130 --> 00:16:14.880
Take care of things.

00:16:15.150 --> 00:16:15.970
Got it.

00:16:16.570 --> 00:16:17.280
Kaoru?

00:16:19.310 --> 00:16:20.510
I'm going to check on things outside.

00:16:23.210 --> 00:16:24.110
I'm going too!

00:16:29.360 --> 00:16:30.220
It's okay.

00:16:35.920 --> 00:16:36.820
What's wrong?

00:16:43.570 --> 00:16:44.360
It's quicksand.

00:16:46.530 --> 00:16:49.230
At this rate, the ship will be swallowed up by the sand.

00:16:50.510 --> 00:16:51.860
Let's go back, Howard.

00:16:58.230 --> 00:16:59.020
Howard!

00:17:05.920 --> 00:17:08.880
Do this, 'n that happens...

00:17:09.180 --> 00:17:11.320
Shingo, this'll take time.

00:17:13.200 --> 00:17:14.730
Chako! Shingo!

00:17:15.410 --> 00:17:17.160
Both of you, hurry up here!

00:17:17.470 --> 00:17:18.900
What'cha sayin'?

00:17:18.900 --> 00:17:20.410
We're up to our elbows here!

00:17:20.770 --> 00:17:21.920
I said hurry!

00:17:25.500 --> 00:17:26.420
Escape?

00:17:26.850 --> 00:17:29.920
Yes, we're getting out of here right away. Get ready.

00:17:30.670 --> 00:17:32.050
We're going to abandon the Orion?

00:17:32.510 --> 00:17:34.010
There's no time. Hurry!

00:17:36.300 --> 00:17:37.060
What's that?

00:17:54.970 --> 00:17:55.530
Adam.

00:17:57.900 --> 00:17:58.570
Luna.

00:18:16.010 --> 00:18:16.890
We're jumping off.

00:18:17.210 --> 00:18:18.030
From here?

00:18:18.220 --> 00:18:19.140
You must be kidding!

00:18:19.760 --> 00:18:21.980
If we wait any longer, we'll just be swallowed up as well!

00:18:25.270 --> 00:18:27.410
Once you jump off, get away from the ship immediately.

00:18:27.600 --> 00:18:28.980
Don't get trapped in the quicksand!

00:18:29.850 --> 00:18:31.200
I'll go first.

00:18:36.070 --> 00:18:37.320
Bell, does it seem okay?

00:18:42.710 --> 00:18:44.580
Everyone, it's okay!

00:18:44.960 --> 00:18:45.630
Alright.

00:18:46.160 --> 00:18:47.280
Let's all go together!

00:18:47.960 --> 00:18:48.520
Adam...

00:18:50.620 --> 00:18:51.410
One...

00:18:52.530 --> 00:18:53.210
Two...

00:18:56.250 --> 00:18:57.090
Three!

00:19:06.600 --> 00:19:07.270
Where's Sharla?

00:19:21.780 --> 00:19:22.580
Sharla!

00:19:28.530 --> 00:19:29.920
Sharla, hang on!

00:19:33.260 --> 00:19:34.120
Sharla!

00:19:35.280 --> 00:19:35.840
Sharla...

00:19:38.430 --> 00:19:39.370
Sorry.

00:19:39.780 --> 00:19:43.530
Let's go home to the colony together, Howard.

00:19:48.670 --> 00:19:49.680
Sharla...

00:19:53.360 --> 00:19:54.530
Howard!

00:19:59.550 --> 00:20:01.280
Howard! Hold on!

00:20:06.600 --> 00:20:07.410
Sharla!

00:20:09.410 --> 00:20:10.420
Howard...

00:20:21.750 --> 00:20:22.420
Okay.

00:20:23.920 --> 00:20:25.060
Be careful, Bell!

00:20:31.980 --> 00:20:33.370
Howard, I...

00:20:35.060 --> 00:20:36.030
Don't give up!

00:20:43.160 --> 00:20:43.990
Howard!

00:20:44.960 --> 00:20:45.540
Bell...

00:20:47.920 --> 00:20:49.310
This is it?

00:20:50.280 --> 00:20:51.210
Stretch your arm out!

00:20:57.750 --> 00:20:59.880
Damn it, so close...

00:21:06.450 --> 00:21:07.350
Howard!

00:21:11.250 --> 00:21:12.730
Howard, your jacket!

00:21:24.260 --> 00:21:25.230
They did it!

00:21:29.430 --> 00:21:31.050
Sharla, hang on!

00:21:38.470 --> 00:21:39.750
Sharla!

00:21:40.160 --> 00:21:41.930
Sharla! Howard!

00:21:47.920 --> 00:21:49.760
Howard, hang on!

00:21:57.820 --> 00:21:58.800
Howard...

00:21:59.580 --> 00:22:02.360
It's okay. Up we go...

00:22:02.580 --> 00:22:04.660
Howard, get away by yourself.

00:22:05.060 --> 00:22:08.060
No way! We're going home to the colony together!

00:22:09.150 --> 00:22:10.160
Howard...

00:22:14.400 --> 00:22:16.380
Howard! Sharla!

00:22:16.650 --> 00:22:17.850
We're coming now!

00:22:18.600 --> 00:22:19.570
We're going home.

00:22:32.580 --> 00:22:34.390
Howard! Sharla!

00:23:03.260 --> 00:23:05.400
It can't be true... It can't be true!

00:23:05.880 --> 00:23:09.000
Howard and Sharla were swallowed up by the quicksand!

00:23:09.220 --> 00:23:10.270
It's my fault.

00:23:10.910 --> 00:23:13.500
If only I'd made the ship better!

00:23:13.610 --> 00:23:15.930
Give it up. It's nobody's fault.

00:23:16.160 --> 00:23:18.150
For now, all we can do is think about living.

00:23:18.480 --> 00:23:19.800
How could...

00:23:20.280 --> 00:23:22.570
How could you be worried about a thing like that?

00:23:22.800 --> 00:23:24.150
You're so cold, Menori!

00:23:25.570 --> 00:23:28.230
Next time: Howard saved us.
